// Phone test notes, Android and iPhone in one file (since 2026-11-20). Preview builds only; the live game never shows them.
// Grouped by test build, newest first (director, 2026-11-20): new lines go under '## New in this build'; when that build is published the heading becomes '## Test build <stamp>' at the next round. Curly apostrophes only. The card opens once per device whenever the
// text changes. Released notes live in notes_release.js.
const TEST_NOTES={v:'test', label:'Test build · '+(window.DL_BUILD==='ios'?'iPhone':'Android'), name:'0.4.9 test build (newest first)', items:[
  '## New in this build',
  'Willow Pond is now a painting: a quiet meadow pond with a great weeping willow, a duck-egg-blue boathouse where you fish from the deck by the door, its rowboat tucked underneath, and a folding chair for Rest mode.',
  'Willow Pond: the willow and the reeds sway, clouds drift, mist lies on the far water in the morning, the pond mirrors the willow and the boathouse, and after dark the windows and lantern glow and fireflies come out.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.24-1854',
  'Homes are no longer customizable: the Your home page, its Home button and its lessons are gone, and every water keeps its home in its standard look. Your old choices stay in your save.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake has a new painted tea house that belongs to the painting: it changes with the light, its shoji door and lantern glow after dark, and it shows in the lake.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: a painted wooden chair stands on the tea house deck; Rest mode sits your angler in it.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.24-0140',
  'Fights: a tired fish much stronger than your tackle now comes in slowly (a fish nearly 3 times your strength about 3.6 times slower), and its second wind clock keeps running, so it usually fights again before you land it.',
  'Fish Frenzy: you can’t cast for 1 second after it ends.',
  'Streaks: the XP bonus climbs half as fast and tops out at the same bonus.',
  'Voyages: setting sail starts you again at level 1 and hands your skills back; you keep the skill points from feats and the Fish Log. Paths stay chosen and work again once you reach their level.',
  'Boons: stronger values across the board, Hot Water also raises rarity, Deep Cooler now adds 6% cooler space a rank at every size, Nest Egg keeps up to 250 million, and a new 18th Boon, Old Habits, starts each voyage at a higher level.',
  'Pearl relics: Head Start is now Quick Study (the first 20 levels need half the XP), Seasoned Angler is now Bounty Ledger (bounties pay 30% more), Angler’s Almanac gives 5 skill points, and three new relics: Sweet Tooth, Feast Bowl and Dusk Lantern.',
  'Rods: the 3 presets are back in Your rods on every device.',
  'Mystery crates can’t be bought with coins any more. Every feat gives one (a big one with a skill point), and bounties can give one.',
  'Bounties can give Nibbles as a bonus.',
  'Aquarium: choose how many Nibbles to feed at once (1x to 100x); a fish eats what you have if it’s fewer. Your Nibbles of each rarity show above your fish.',
  'Aquarium: sort your fish like the Cooler (oldest, newest, rarity, income, species).',
  'Inspect on every fish in the Cooler and the Aquarium opens its fish card: weight, value, income, boost, Nibbles eaten, mastery and your record.',
  'Shiny and mythic fish pictures: the glow stays around the fish instead of filling the whole picture.',
  'Music: the clicking in many tracks is gone (the lo-fi record crackle and the clicks at the start of notes), and the wave sound no longer clicks when it loops.',
  'Learn and Help in Quests are updated for the game as it is now: fights, Nibbles, homes, voyages, the last waters, crates and bounties.',

  '## Test build 2026.11.23-2143',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: the sky lanterns all come in from the left, fly in front of the mountains, and glow more softly. Rain rings on the water are easier to see.',
  'Fights: legendaries come back to 75% fight on their first second wind and mythics to full fight.',
  'Fights: a fish stronger than your line has twice the fight, puts 1.5 times the strain on the line and takes 1.5 times the line on runs and jumps.',
  'Fights: jumps can chain like darts (jumpers more often), head shakes are a little stronger on less rare fish, and a rare-or-better fish hooked on a cast of 65% or less pulls line for its first 3 to 5 seconds.',
  'Fights: in waters too shallow for dives, divers make a short dive and their runs and darts last longer.',
  'Fights: small hybrids fight like ones of their usual size, the float stays where the fish really is, and the line runs out at 80 m (the Deep Spool attachment adds more).',
  'Fight wording: It’s about to run! / Darting!, Careful… / Jumping!, Get ready… / Reel!, Watch out… / Head Shake!. The Swimming in text is gone (the arrows stay).',
  'Legendary and mythic hybrids are worth more, and shiny, titled and hybrid bonuses all stack on one fish.',
  'Rods cost far more Scales to buy and far more coins to upgrade; the rarest rod’s last upgrade is 10,000,000.',
  'Updated fishing and oddity hints, and the help about snapped lines.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-2049',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: no more white lines in the water where the clouds are reflected.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: the sky lanterns now drift across the sky from left to right, climbing as they go, at many distances and sizes, a few at a time and spread out (near ones in front of the hills, far ones behind them), and each is mirrored as a lantern in the lake.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: cloud reflections stay behind the mountains’ reflections, and the sun no longer leaves a path on the water (the moon still does).',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-2023',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: the clouds, the sun and the moon now reflect in the lake, with a shimmering path of light under the sun or moon.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: white paper sky lanterns rise into the night sky, near ones lifting off in front of the hills and far ones behind them, and their glow shows in the water. The lanterns floating on the lake are gone.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: rain makes rings on the water, the ripples are a little stronger and grow in rain and storms, and the birds now fly behind the big cherry tree.',
  'The moon is a clean crescent on every water (it showed a faint ring around its dark side).',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1945',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: no more blur at dusk and dawn. The dusk and night lighting are now laid over the day painting’s exact shapes, so the changing light never doubles up.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: new reflections made from the scenery itself, so the bridge, torii, pagoda, waterfall, islands and Fuji are mirrored exactly under themselves, in the light of the time of day, fading with depth.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: no more leaping fish.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1901',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: the light now changes smoothly through dawn and dusk, with no blur or sudden steps.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: the reflections line up with what they mirror, the waterfall flows without visible repeating pieces and stays inside its painted water, and the line across a hill is gone.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: the koi and the swirling ribbon of petals are gone.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1827',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake now uses a new layered painting: clouds drift slowly behind the mountains, the lake and its reflections ripple, the big cherry tree sways and the shore flowers nod.',
  'The scene changes properly with the time of day: a cool pink dawn, a bright day, a warm dusk with peach clouds and pink reflections, and a moonlit night where the hills, trees and Fuji are relit in blue and the water darkens.',
  'The sky, sun, moon and stars now show behind the painted mountains and trees, and the water picks up the color of the sky.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1655',
  'At high tension, a calm fish (low temper) lets the tension fall faster when you ease up, up to twice as fast.',
  'Darts chain less often, more for rarer fish: a common fish rarely chains darts, a mythic always chains two or three.',
  'Long runs back to back: each long run is shorter than the one before, until 3 seconds pass after a long run or the fish does something else.',
  'Rod length, Reel, Line, Hook and Cooler now share one price curve: 250, 2,500, 10,000, 36,000, 75,000, 225,000, 675,000, 2,000,000, 6,000,000, 15,000,000 (Line’s extra 11th level: 35,000,000).',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1543',
  'Some icons showed as an empty box on older PCs and phones (the bait reward on daily tasks, the Bait tab, Boardwalk coins): they use icons every device has now.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1521',
  'Less grace at full tension: the line now snaps after about a third of a second of reeling at 100% (was half a second).',
  'Long runs: every 3 good pulls in rhythm give +1 combo and shorten the run (was every 5).',
  'Tired Rare, Epic, Legendary and Mythic fish come in a little slower.',
  'Second Bite has 10 ranks: one more try per bite at ranks 1, 5 and 10. Its rare odds boost lasts only for that cast and ends once a fish is hooked or your tries run out.',
  'Tackle upgrades now start at level 0 and every one goes to at least level 10: Hook and Fish Finder have more, smaller steps, and Rod length and Cooler gained a new top level. New prices for every upgrade, climbing to a much higher top.',
  'Attachments have five tiers (were three) and cost more: 5,000, 25,000, 125,000, 625,000 and 3,000,000 coins.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1252',
  'A fish with a full temper bar punishes reeling: tension builds faster and faster as the bar fills past half, up to 2.5 times as fast when it is full.',
  'Special fish fight harder: a shiny a little harder, a titled fish by its kind (Rainbow, then Starry, Spectral, Ancient), and a hybrid by its size, big ones much harder.',
  'Small hybrids keep more of their worth: they lose only half the sale value their low weight would cost, and earn in the aquarium as if they weighed the usual amount.',
  'During runs the fight only says “It’s darting” or “It’s running!”.',
  'The band that stops a dive is 15% narrower.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1223',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake comes alive: the lake’s reflections ripple, the painted waterfall flows with foam and mist at its foot, the big cherry tree sways and the shore flowers nod in the breeze.',
  'Life on the lake: koi glide through the clear shallows, birds cross the sky, butterflies flutter over the flowers, dragonflies dart and hover, a fish leaps now and then, sunlight glints on the water and fireflies come out at night.',
  'Your tea house now mirrors in the lake, its paper lanterns are proper chochin with ribs, caps and tassels that glow warm, and the lily pads float in front of its posts.',
  'Stars and the moon now stay in the open sky, behind Fuji and the hills.',
  'The swirl of petals on the breeze is all pink now, so it no longer looks like little white fish.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1201',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake now uses your newest painting: hills full of cherry trees, the near shore with mossy stones, flowers and clear water, the lake, bridge, waterfall, pagoda and torii, all painted.',
  'Your house stands on a full set of posts along its whole deck, with cross braces, a beam under the deck and a tie beam through the posts.',
  'The waterfall runs with falling water that speeds up as it drops, foam at its foot and drifting mist.',
  'At night the floating lights on the lake are Japanese paper lanterns (toro nagashi) on wooden floats, glowing with trembling reflections.',
  'The sun’s sparkle and the drifting petals on the lake now start below the islands, never on the rocks.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-1132',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake now uses your painted picture as its scenery: Fuji, the cherry trees, the red bridge and island, the waterfall and pagoda, the torii and the lotus, all painted. Your house, angler, line and the lake’s moving life are drawn on top.',
  'The painting follows the time of day and weather: warm at dusk, dark blue at night with stars, the moon and the pagoda’s lit windows; the waterfall still runs.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0856',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake, rebuilt to the director’s corrected picture: clear blue water and sky, Fuji right of centre, the house with warm glowing shoji walls standing on its deck over open water, the big cherry tree over it, the red bridge to a little island, rocky islets with cherry trees along the far shore, the waterfall and its pavilion right of centre with the pagoda on the hill above, the torii on its rocks to the right, and lotus clusters in the near water. The lantern path and the stone-step corner from the earlier picture are gone.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0815',
  'The Nile: your reed boat is redrawn the way Egyptian paintings show it: a crescent hull of papyrus bundles with rope lashings, slim horns at both ends rising to papyrus flower heads (gold lotus on the gilded barque, with a painted eye), a steering oar at the stern, and a cabin on lotus columns, a temple pylon or a striped tent. Your saved choices carry over.',
  'Circuit Lake, redone in its own style: your home is a capsule pod hovering on its pad, with a glowing round window, a neon sign on the roof, an antenna and a vending machine beside it (or a noodle stall with red lanterns, or an arcade booth). Pick the home, the sign’s words, pad, thrusters, trim, light and seat in Your home.',
  'Mount Olympus, redone in its own style: your home is a small marble temple on a stepped base over the clouds, with Doric, Ionic or Corinthian columns, a pediment with a gold sun relief, plain marble or a painted frieze, gold ornaments at its corners, and a statue of Zeus, Athena or Poseidon inside. Clouds drift around the posts.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0800',
  'Corporate Pond, redone in its own style: your home is a modernist glass pavilion on steel columns in the reflecting pool, with a thin roof slab and the company logo, steel frames, and the office visible inside (a desk and glowing monitor, a ficus and water cooler, or a whiteboard of charts). A concrete planter and a coffee cup sit on the deck. Your partition and lamp choices carry over.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0757',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake, redrawn to the director’s picture: Fuji large and to the right, a big cherry tree painted in thousands of petals over the house, a grassy bank behind the house whose stone path climbs away to the red bridge with its fence and lantern posts getting smaller with distance, cherry trees on that bank, a little island past the bridge, a forested cliff with the waterfall and its pavilion, a row of cherries on the right shore, a larger torii on its rocks, and pink flowers in the bottom-left corner.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0749',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake, rebuilt to match the director’s picture: the house has a low, wide roof of dark grey tiles with a heavy ridge over glowing shoji walls and round windows, on brown wooden posts, with a much bigger cherry tree spilling over it.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: blue ridges and forested hills in front of Fuji, a waterfall from a rocky cliff with a small pavilion on top, a red arched bridge, a fenced stone path with lantern posts along the left shore, the torii on a rocky islet, the pagoda on the right-hand hill, more pink lotus, koi shadows under the near water, and a bigger near corner with wide stone steps, two wooden lanterns, a rope fence and pink flowers. Lanterns glow at night.',
  'The Buffet, redone in its own style: your home is a gingerbread house with a steep roof under dripping icing and gumdrops, candy-cane corners and a peppermint window, on a silver platter; a giant fork with a cherry stands in the soup beside it. Your trim and candle choices carry over.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0737',
  'Animal Farm, redone in its own style: your home is a red barn with the classic two-pitch barn roof and white trim, a hayloft with a hoist and a bundle of hay, and big white X-braced doors (or a Dutch door, or doors rolled open with hay inside). A grassy bank with a hay stack and sunflowers runs behind it. Your fence and lantern choices carry over.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0727',
  'Starfall Lake, redone in its own style: your home is a round star observatory of moonstone with a crystal, silver or star-blossom dome and a gold star on top, a moon-shaped door and a frieze of tiny constellations, standing on a floating rock island with crystals hanging beneath. Your telescope and star lantern choices carry over.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0716',
  'Ember Springs, redone in its own style: your home is a basalt bathhouse on hexagonal basalt columns rising from the hot water, with a curved iron barrel roof, round windows that glow at night, a vent that lets off steam, and the steaming pool beside it. Pick the walls, roof, door, hot pool, lantern and seat in Your home.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0706',
  'Hollow Trench, redone in its own style: your home is a castaway raft of tarred barrels and salvaged planks lashed with rope, glowing growth on the barrels below the water. Its shelter is the wrecked lifeboat of a lost ship turned upside down on props (or a sailcloth tent over an oar, or a crooked plank shack with a ship’s porthole). Your raft, mast, salvage and lantern choices carry over.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0655',
  'Midnight Deep: your trawler is rebuilt as a working steel stern trawler: a deep hull with a high bulwark, freeing ports with rust streaks below them, old tyres hung as fenders, her name and number, a towering wheelhouse forward, and a net drum wound with net and orange floats (or a stern gantry with a trawl door, or stacked crab pots). Your saved choices carry over.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0645',
  'Amazon Rainforest, redone in its own style: your home is a palafito, a stilt house high on vine-lashed poles with a very steep thatched roof hanging low over its walls. Pick the walls, roof, door, river gear, lamp and seat in Your home.',
  'Amazon Rainforest: a notched log ladder climbs down to the water, giant water lilies with red rims float around the stilts, and the buttress roots of a huge tree reach in from the left.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0634',
  'Brine Shelf: your boat is rebuilt as a big-game sport-fisher, stern toward the fish: a tall hull with chrome rails, a transom door and swim platform, her name on the side, a cabin with a raked windscreen, portholes and a life ring, and a flybridge with a ladder (or a wheelhouse, or a tuna tower) with outriggers splayed out. Your saved choices carry over.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0624',
  'Florida Keys: your skiff is rebuilt as a real flats skiff, bow toward the fish: a low fiberglass hull with a rub rail, a stripe at the waterline and its registration, an outboard on the back, a center console with a windscreen (or a poling platform, or a tiller boat), and a T-top, bimini or umbrella. It is staked out with a push pole in the sand. Your saved choices carry over.',
  'Florida Keys: a green channel marker stands in the flats with a pelican resting on top; its light blinks green at night.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0610',
  'Coral Shallows, redone in its own style: your home is an overwater bungalow high on palm stilts, with a tall thatched roof, a shaggy fringe and a little vent at the top. Pick the walls, roof, door, windows, beach gear, torch and seat in Your home.',
  'Coral Shallows: a ladder goes down into the clear water, the sandbar with coral and a starfish shows through under the bungalow, and a coconut palm leans out over the roof.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0600',
  'Frostbite Lake, redone in its own style: your home is a timber ice shanty on sled skids, with a snow-capped roof and icicles, a stovepipe with smoke and a window that glows at night. Pick the walls, roof, stovepipe, door, windows, gear and seat in Your home.',
  'Frostbite Lake: snow drifts against the shanty, footprints lead to a tip-up flag over its hole, and a box sled waits beside it.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0547',
  'Saltmarsh Coast, redone in its own style: your home is a tall saltbox lobster shack at the end of the pier, with a stovepipe, buoys on its wall (or stacked lobster pots, or a net drying on a pole). Pick the siding, roof, door, windows, gear, lamp and seat in Your home.',
  'Saltmarsh Coast: the pier stands on tall tarred pilings with cross bracing, barnacles and weed at the tide line; a ladder goes down to a dory tied at the end, and a gull stands on the mooring post. A bell buoy rocks offshore (its light blinks at night).',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0534',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake, redone in its own style: your home is a tea house raised on red-lacquered posts, with a layered roof whose eaves curve up at the tips, shoji walls between dark posts, paper lanterns under the eaves and a rope railing along the veranda. Pick the walls, roof, lanterns, railing, door, windows and seat in Your home.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: a big cherry tree frames the corner over your roof, and a mossy bank with a stone path, bamboo fence and azaleas runs behind the tea house down to the water.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: a mossy stone corner in the bottom right with steps down into the water, a stone lantern that glows at night, a rope fence and pink lotus flowers on their stems.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0507',
  'Stonebrook River, redone in its own style: your home is a two-storey stone mill house over the mill race, the river running through its arch, a dormer with a hoist and flour sack (or a window, or a pigeon loft), a steep roof and a chimney; choose walls, roof, dormer, chimney, door, windows and seat. Around it: a stone retaining wall with steps, ferns and foxgloves.',
  'Stonebrook River: a fly fisher wades mid-river in his waders, casting in loops (he goes home at night).',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0450',
  'Willow Pond: the ground around the boathouse is its own now: a grassy slope with a gravel path down to the deck, a split-rail fence, lupines and daisies, pines and a young maple, and cattails in the shallows.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0440',
  'Willow Pond, redone in its own style: your home is a tall red boathouse over the water with a cupola and weathervane, its boat bay at the waterline (a canoe inside, swing doors or a sliding door) and a lean-to porch beside it; choose its walls, roof, cupola, boat bay, windows, lantern and seat.',
  'Willow Pond: the far cabin has its own little jetty with a rowboat tied up, and a rope swing hangs under the willow.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0418',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: your home is now a tea house on red-lacquered posts you customise: walls (shoji, plaster and timber, bamboo), roof (curved clay tiles, cypress bark, copper), lantern (paper, stone, a string of lanterns), shade (veranda roof, wisteria trellis, paper parasol), door (sliding shoji, plank, noren curtain), windows and seat, with cherry trees in blossom behind it.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0403',
  'Stonebrook River: your home is now a stone mill shed on fieldstone piers you customise: walls, roof (slate, shakes or thatch), chimney with smoke, lantern, door, windows and seat, with autumn woods on the bank behind it.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0352',
  'Willow Pond: your home is now a pine boathouse you customise: walls, roof, lantern, shade (including the patio umbrella), door, windows and seat, on a pine bank with round piles. Your seat sits at the deck’s edge.',
  'Willow Pond: the weeping willow is green again by day.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0332',
  'Fixed: a brand-new save no longer loses most of its Wisdom Pearls the first time the game reloads.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0322',
  'New skill, Second Bite: one more try per bite at ranks 3, 6 and 9, better rare odds on every try after a miss, and at full rank a missed hotspot bite doesn’t break your streak. Water Reader no longer gives the extra try.',
  'Gourmet: fish caught on their favourite food also sell for more (6% a rank).',
  'Naturalist is now a mastery skill: each mastery star adds a little more value, and at full rank the first star comes at 2 catches.',
  'Candy Maker goes up to rank 10, and each rank gives a small chance that the Nibbles from scrapping are a rarity higher.',
  'Snag Sense says what it does: better at avoiding snags.',
  'End-game waters open one voyage sooner: Animal Farm after your first voyage, and one more after each voyage.',
  'Loading a save code takes you back to the fishing screen to confirm the load.',
  'Fixed: the cooler’s Sell choices now always decide (the rarity menu, Sell shinies too and Sell hybrids too were overruled by Protect rare fish); the rarity menu no longer closes by itself.',
  'Fixed: landing a reward in a fight no longer makes the float jump; the line it wins back comes in smoothly.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0259',
  'Fishing feel: runs come a little less often, short darting runs are more common than long ones, and a fish rests at least a moment after a run instead of chaining runs back to back.',
  'Long runs: each good short pull ends the run sooner, and the combo grows every 5 good pulls. Darting runs have fewer darts in a row (a few more for the rarest fish).',
  'Fish have a little more fight, and a tired fish gets its second wind a bit sooner.',
  'A rare or rarer fish hooked close to you (within 40% of a cast) surges and takes line for its first 3 seconds, more the rarer it is.',
  'Fixed: the screen no longer turns white while you reel in junk and oddities.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0124',
  'Canadian Rockies, from your latest notes: the lake floor now shows only in the shallows near you and drops away into deep water, so fights happen out over the deep.',
  'The otter’s head joins its body when it sits on the rock, and it swims in above the boulder and the log instead of through them.',
  'The rocks, the log and the reeds in the near corners sit in the water: their underwater parts take the water’s color and a bright line rings them at the surface.',
  'Your cabin’s chimney smokes; the stone base reaches out under the log ends so the corners line up; the bank under the cabin is one grassy slope with moss, ferns and stones; the Muskoka chair’s parts all join.',
  'Geese fly over in different flocks each time: V, lopsided V, a single line or a loose skein, either way across.',
  'The canoeist pulls up his canoe at dusk, walks to his cabin and goes in; at dawn he walks back out.',
  'The waterfall now has a source: a mountain stream winds down the forested slope from a snowfield, white over its rapids, and pours over the cliff. The beaver sits on its dam. The blue glacier on the mountain and the birches are gone (they don’t belong at this lake).',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0053',
  'Fishing feel: Middle is now the game’s feel for everyone (Cam: “the one for sure”). Your Feel lab settings start fresh on Middle.',
  'Temper builds much faster the longer you keep reeling and cools faster the longer you ease off, and the hotter the fish, the harder its moves pull the line tight.',
  'Two kinds of runs: darting runs are short sharp bursts that zigzag (let them go and the fish tires itself), long runs pull steadily for several seconds (short pulls in rhythm win line back and build your combo).',
  'In the groove: between moves, keep the line between 50% and 80% while you reel and the fish comes in faster.',
  'Landing a big one now ends with a big splash and a little fanfare.',
  'A predator that swallows your catch no longer races off the screen: it runs out at most 45 m for the rarest, less for commoner ones, never past 50 m.',
  'The “Reel hard!” moment before a second wind is a little shorter.',
  'Feel lab has three new knobs: Temper curve, Darting and long runs, Groove bonus.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.23-0034',
  'Canadian Rockies, from your notes: the mountains now show layered rock with snow lying on the ledges, the snowfields end without teeth or steps, and the forested mountainsides have the same layered rock instead of white triangles.',
  'The lake is crystal clear: you can see the stony lake floor, rounded stones in tan, rust, grey and cream, big and clear near you and fading into the turquoise far out.',
  'The far shore is a thin green bank with shrubs and boulders instead of a pink beach; the spruces have real branches; the cabin’s stone chimney stands behind its roof; the waterfall cliff is layered rock with spruces on top.',
  'The beaver dam no longer has water sparkle running across it, and the floating green patches by the waterfall are gone.',
  'The canoeist paddles home to his cabin as night falls and paddles out again at dawn.',
  'A river otter now lives in the near left corner, with a fallen log, a boulder and a bed of sedges: it swims in, dives, eats a crayfish floating on its back, climbs onto the boulder to groom, and swims off through the sedges.',
  'Your log cabin: Door and Windows are now two separate parts; Squared timbers became Dovetailed timbers with flush corners; Whitewashed chinking became Logs on a stone base; Green tin became Tin roof in any color; a real sod roof with grass hanging over the eave and wildflowers; more colors for every part.',
  'Chimneys: stones and bricks stay inside the chimney; the stovepipe has joints, a damper, a storm collar and a rain cap.',
  'New seats: a real Muskoka chair, a stump with a striped wool blanket, and a rocker built from logs. Your seat now sits at the edge of the deck, close to the water.',
  'The posts under the cabin carry straight on down into the water instead of jumping sideways at the surface.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.22-2337',
  'Canadian Rockies cabin, checked in every combination: the covered porch now has a real shed roof in the cabin roof’s own material, with a shadow on the wall, so you can see it.',
  'The Rockies cabin keeps its real proportions on every screen: lower walls and a low roof, and on phones it carries on past the left edge as one long lodge instead of a tall, squeezed box.',
  'The porch’s log rail now runs in front of you, your chair and your pet, instead of behind them.',
  'Dutch door and window box now gives both windows a flower box; shuttered windows have louvred shutters in the door’s color that stand out from the logs.',
  'Each cabin part offers only colors a real cabin would have (no turquoise logs or snow-white roofs).',
  'The old snow on the forested mountainsides now lies in long streaks down the gullies instead of round patches.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.22-2306',
  'Canadian Rockies, rebuilt by itself with full care: a jagged row of snowy peaks with a glacier, forested mountainsides with larches and avalanche paths, rose snow at dusk and a dim navy night, a canoe dock with red canoes, fireweed and granite on the near shore.',
  'Your home at the Rockies is now a log cabin you customise: log walls, roof (cedar shakes, green tin, sod with wildflowers), chimney, porch (open, covered, or with a log rail), door and windows (they glow at night), and seat.',
  'The cabin stands on a granite ledge and braced log posts that sit on the rock and on boulders under the water.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.22-2221',
  'Tester tools › Feel lab: try the fight with different settings, live. Presets: Old, Current (Cam’s update), Middle and Arcade; then change any number with − and +. Kept on this device.',
  'New in the fight (Middle and Arcade): shorter fights; a short warning before a run, a shake or a dive; the right reaction pays (ease off in runs and shakes, reel when it jumps or swims toward you, hold the dive band).',
  'Perfect pull: as a move ends the float glows for a moment. Press reel right then and the fish loses a chunk of its fight.',
  'Combo: right reactions in a row speed up your reel (up to +40%); reeling into a move at the snap line resets it. A hook flash and short pop-ups show how you did.',
  'You can now see when a fish swims toward you (arrows by the float, “Swimming in, reel!”), and second winds come sooner.',
  'The Fishing: New / Old switch is now the Old preset in the Feel lab.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.22-2051',
  'Every water redone: new scenery shapes of its own (no more shared mountains), and things that floated now stand on something.',
  'Willow Pond: a forest ridge instead of mountains, the deer walks on the bank, ducks leave a real wake, a livelier frog.',
  'Stonebrook River: the arches show the hills behind, leaves drift downstream, farmland on the hills; a mooring post replaces the dock waterwheel.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake: two giant cherry trees in front of Mount Fuji, a second pagoda, a clearer torii; lanterns and ducks come in from the edges.',
  'Saltmarsh Coast: terraced fields and a harbour under the village, beach huts by the lighthouse.',
  'Frostbite Lake: taller mountains with real shape; it snows here instead of raining. Canadian Rockies: layered mountains, golden larches.',
  'Many more waters got new details: stilt houses, a sea arch, cinder cones, a farmhouse, a landmark tower, a mud-brick village and more.',
  'Homes: options are clearly different, none borrowed from another water, and covers keep the rain off you; the resting rod stays under covers.',
  'Supports under every home have shape now (caps, wet bands, bracing). Lantern colors show by day too.',
  'The aurora is smooth and sits behind the clouds, stars no longer shine through clouds, and the rainbow’s reflection lines up.',
  '## Test build 2026.11.22-1735',
  'Tester tools (Stats): new Time and weather buttons. Jump to dawn, day, dusk or night, or to any weather, at once; Real time puts the clock back. The jump is kept when you reload.',
  'Travel works while you rest (you keep resting at the new water); with a line out, Travel says to reel in first instead of doing nothing.',
  'Waters you have opened are never called Uncharted Waters any more.',
  'Fish named after a real fish (tuna, mackerel, marlin, sole, moonfish, puffer and many more) now have that fish’s body in the newer waters, instead of a random shape.',
  'The main teal buttons are a touch deeper, so their white text is easier to read.',
  'Behind the scenes: every water’s drawing now lives in a file of its own (20 files), checked to draw pixel for pixel the same at day and at night. Nothing should look different; tell us if anything does.',
  '## Test build 1447',
  'Fish no longer wear their water’s costume: the headdresses, ankhs, laurels, ties, glasses, ears, horns, food toppings and circuit lines are gone. Every fish is drawn as just the fish.',
  'Map: clearer wording. The top line says how to open the next water (or that all are open), each card says how strong your line is and how many of its fish that covers, and the count reads “2 of 52 caught”.',
  'Your home: the 16 colors are real circles like the old canopy colors, 2 rows of 8, and look the same for every feature (the lantern colors no longer glow).',
  '## Test build 0540',
  'Fish: real fish families look like themselves: catfish get their whiskers and flat heads, the tiger shovelnose is a striped catfish, arowana and arapaima are long and scaled, piranhas have teeth, cichlids, oscars, discus, tetras, plecos, loaches, snakeheads, gobies, lungfish and bichirs have their real shapes and markings.',
  'Long fish are slim: arowanas, loaches, plecos, bichirs and snakeheads, and the Nile electric catfish is a catfish (it was drawn like a sunfish).',
  'The black ghost knifefish and the black phantom tetra are dark fish now, not see-through.',
  'Opening the game in a browser (not the installed app) shows a welcome with how to install it on this device, every time; Settings › Install Driftline brings it back.',
  'The install welcome waits until other cards (like these notes) are closed.',
  'Dawn, dusk and weather changes: the scenery’s new light is painted a little at a time, and the mountains are much cheaper to paint, so the short freezes when the light changes should be gone. Tell us if you still see one.',
  'Behind the scenes: each water’s extra scenery (boats, birds, lights, waves) now has one owner instead of layers stacked on layers. Nothing should look different; tell us if anything does.',
  '## Test build 0407',
  'Save › Backup on this device: your progress is copied every few minutes and whenever you leave the game; Restore brings it back (tap twice). If your progress suddenly drops, the better copy is kept as an earlier backup.',
  'Behind the scenes: tidier code for the Map, Skills, Pets, Trophy Room and Events pages. Nothing should look different; tell us if anything does.',
  '## Test build 0351',
  'Your home: color buttons have a faint light ring, so the darkest colors stay visible.',
  '## Test build 0305',
  'Roofs, umbrellas, sheds and tents now cover you: each one reaches from before your seat to past where you stand, and stands tall enough to clear your hat.',
  'Covers are drawn from the side: the umbrella is a cap on a pole, the lean-to is one roof line.',
  'Posts and supports blend into the water: murky under the surface, fading out a short way down.',
  'Stonebrook River: the waterwheel turns under the landing beside the mill shed instead of hanging off the end.',
  'The Home preview always shows your whole home, roof included.',
  'Map pictures appear much faster, show each water’s own home, stay saved when you travel, and are also made while you rest.',
  'A water you visit for the first time starts with its own home’s look instead of copying the last one.',
  'Your home: the colors are round buttons again, 2 rows of 8, and the page reaches the top of the screen.',
  'Fishmonger’s Gamble: very long fish names wrap inside their button instead of spilling onto the one below.',
  '## Test build 0145',
  'Every water now has its own home, made from that water’s look and story: a mill landing with a waterwheel, a tea house deck, a pier end, an ice camp, a lodge ledge, a beach hut, a flats skiff, a sport-fishing boat, a stilt house, a trawler, a salvage raft, a bathhouse, a crystal platform, a barn dock, a gingerbread platter, an office deck, a reed boat, a hover pad and a temple porch.',
  'Every home has a seat plus 5 parts of its own, 3 styles each, and one list of 16 colors. Boats, rafts and platforms bob on the water. Resting sits you in your seat.',
  'Every water has its own music now (12 new themes), and each plays softer at night.',
  'Home decorations and the cozy bonus are gone (decorations were cheap and every home part is free). The Tide Pass gives aquarium decorations instead, and the Homebody path is now Pet Nap: while you rest, your pets nap beside you and their bond grows by itself.',
  'Your home at Willow Pond, reworked from the director’s notes: 6 parts (Light, Deck, Posts, Rail, Canopy and a new Seat), 3 styles each, and one list of 16 colors shared by every part so pieces can match.',
  'New styles: a log deck, round piles with rope, a low log rail, a lean-to roof and a sailcloth shade (drawn from the side like the umbrella), and three seats: a camp chair, a log bench and a deck chair. Resting sits you in your seat.',
  'The posts run all the way down and fade into the water, the water flows past them instead of rings growing and shrinking, and the umbrella stands on the deck instead of the rail.',
  'The Home preview shows just your home. Where you are is a small label on the view; the strip under it is gone.',
  '## Test build 2338',
  'Cam’s fish feel update: tension builds a little while you reel and only falls when you stop (steadily, slower during a move). Temper empties in about 3 s once you stop; a fish at full temper moves up to 3 times as often (each move costs it less Fight). Reeling into a move drains its Fight faster.',
  'Between moves a fish sometimes swims toward you for a moment: reel faster then. Tired fish come in faster, most for common fish.',
  'Second winds: rare and epic fish can get one more, legendary and mythic two more, each a coin flip while the fish is tired, so a fish can no longer just be waited out.',
  'Dives (deep waters) are a third of runs, last 5-20 s and stop once you keep the tension in the band for 1.5 s; they pull line more slowly but can take far more. The spool holds 200 m.',
  'A perfect hook holds the fish still for 1.5 s. “Careful!” shows when the fish’s temper is high enough to make it move quickly.',
  'Fights are a little faster overall (first version, tell us how it feels). Rarer oddities reel in more slowly.',
  'The hooked fish’s shadow is one even tone when it turns away to take line too (it showed darker fins and tail).',
  '## Test build 2301',
  'Wardrobe › Tide Pass: the aura previews are bigger and stay bright while locked, so you can see each aura before you reach it.',
  'Empty Cooler: a picture, what the Cooler is for, and a Go fishing button instead of a mostly blank page.',
  'Boardwalk: Mystery crates has a picture like the other games, and Higher or lower keeps its picture after a game.',
  'Fishmonger’s Gamble: after a play the fish buttons sit two to a row and the result lines up with them, so the card no longer grows past the screen (a long name wraps inside its button; the price always shows). With an empty cooler the card shows its picture like the other games.',
  'Catch cards always show what you caught: after a shiny or mythic fish, the next card (an oddity, say) kept showing that fish.',
  'Fish pictures in lists (Cooler, Aquarium, Fish Log) no longer blank for a moment when the scroll bar fades: phones use their own scroll bar now.',
  'The side panel stays on screen while a catch card is showing (it vanished).',
  'Cooler: a Hybrids switch beside Shinies in the Sell all filter. Off keeps hybrids when you Sell all or Scrap all; it starts like Shinies.',
  'Aquarium boosts show what you really get: a titled shiny’s lift on the other fish now counts on the Aquarium page, in each fish’s line and on the catch card (they showed less than you got). A new species’ catch card shows that fish’s own boost, not the species’ average.',
  'Settings: the Download for Windows button is gone from test builds (it gave the live app; play the test build in the browser instead).',
  '## Test build 1549',
  'Living maps, every water held to the map standard: Willow Pond, a mother duck leads 3 to 5 ducklings across the far water by day and a tawny owl glides low over the pond at night (every 50 s). Saltmarsh Coast, a pod of porpoises rolls past (every 42 s). Ember Springs, a geyser at the foot of the hill erupts (every 45 s, a little higher or lower each time) and ravens circle by day. Animal Farm, fireflies by the fence and a barn owl at night, birds only by day, the tractor every 55 s. The Nile, fruit bats at night. Corporate Pond, pigeons strut on the ticker by day. The Buffet, a gummy bear rows a cracker across the lake. Stonebrook otters every 24 s.',
  'Moments made bigger so they read on a phone: the leaping fish at Florida Keys, the meatball at The Buffet, the paper plane at Corporate Pond, the whale tail at Midnight Deep and the eyes at Hollow Trench.',
  'Rain that fits the water: sprinkles fall at The Buffet, stardust at Starfall Lake and Mount Olympus (rain and storms elsewhere as before).',
  'Starfall Lake draws almost twice as fast (its fish constellation is drawn once instead of every frame). Looks the same.',
  'Behind the scenes, no look change: the Aquarium, Cooler, Settings, Save, Your home and Rods pages are each built in one place now. The Cooler no longer builds a hidden help box, and Rods no longer adds a new watcher on every redraw. Tell us if anything on these pages looks or acts differently.',
  'Tester tools › Run every check: time limits stretch on slower phones (the report says by how much), and a new Maps check runs every water at dawn, day, dusk and night in every weather.',
  '## Test build 0720',  'Quests › Goals now shows the live event when one is on (it never appeared before).',
  'Feats: each category heading says what finishing it gives.',
  'Bounties: the daily tasks card no longer shows under the other tabs on wide screens.',
  'Quiet Waters: no more notices on the fishing screen when the weather changes, an event goes live, special weather is coming or a challenge starts (the badges and LIVE marker show them). Messages about what you just did stay, jokes included. The Weather pop-ups setting is gone with them.',
  'Florida Keys, first part of Cam’s list: a bigger bridge between the keys with traffic (cars, minivans, box trucks, semis; lights at night), beaches under the keys, speedboats and sport-fishing boats ripping by, and a school of fish under the water. No gulls at night.',
  'Amazon, from Cam’s list: a deep rainforest with tall trees, cliff ledges with moss and boulders, the waterfall now ends in a foaming pool, an island that narrows the channel, roots and lily pads along the banks; dragonflies, butterflies, macaws, a caiman, a bullfrog, drifting branches and poison dart frogs on the front leaves; once a minute the river dolphin, an anaconda swimming or a basilisk running on the water. The stilt deck stands in the water now (it ran to the bottom of the screen) and its roof has real posts.',
  '## Test build 0509',
  'Cam’s fight feel (the new fishing): fish rest between moves (head shakes, runs, jumps, and dives in deep water); a fish’s weight decides what its moves can do (small fish can’t take line, big ones can); rare fish chain moves; a tired fish gets one Second wind. Reel in short pulls during a move. A cast to the far edge is 40 m, a fish 150 m out takes all your line, and 10 seconds without reeling lets it swim off.',
  'Dives (waters 100 m deep or more): the ring around the fish shows a pink band; keep the line inside it to cut the dive short.',
  'Jumps go toward you (reel now) or away from you (let go). A running fish turns at once, no slow flip.',
  'Bites: one try per bite to start; Quick Reflexes (ranks 5 and 10) and a full Water Reader each add one. Miss every try at a hotspot and the fish takes your bait and your streak.',
  'Compare the two: Stats › Tester tools › Fishing: New / Old (test builds only).',
  'Oddities reel in faster, and their first snag comes sooner. Rod length now shows its rare odds (every cast reaches 40 m at the far edge).',
  'Hollow Trench is 3,000 m+ deep and its fish are stronger than Midnight Deep’s.',
  'End-game waters stay Uncharted Waters until you reach their voyage, then open for coins and stay open for good (waters you already have stay open).',
  'Cooler: Scrap all sits beside Sell all, and a new Rarity sort. Settings: distances and depths in metres or feet.',
  'Fixes: the Bounties badge no longer shows a number with nothing to claim; scrap messages name the Nibble tier; feeding a Nibble no longer makes the screen jump; Map pictures show at once after a restart; Pets › Customize keeps the Hat color and Accessory color rows in place (greyed out when they don’t apply).',
  '## Test build 0159',
  'Willow Pond home, changed from your notes: no grassy bank (the home stands on its own); lanterns are now a lamp post, a hurricane lantern on the boards and a firefly jar; canopies are an open sky, a patio umbrella, a cloth pergola or a wooden shelter, all drawn from the side; rails gained an iron rail; stone piers sit exactly under the deck; the water rings no longer cross the posts; the Home close-up is sharp (the angler and pet were blurry).',
  'Color is now spelled color everywhere in the game.',
  '## Test build 0114',
  'Pilot of the new homes, at Willow Pond only: the dock now starts from a grassy bank, and Your home has 5 parts to change (Lantern, Deck, Posts, Rail, Canopy), 3 styles and 6 colors each, all free. The Home view zooms in on your home. Decorations and moving pets don’t apply there (they go when every home is converted). Every other water keeps its old home for now.',
  'Phones: color choices on pages with tabs no longer show under the wrong tab.',
  '## Test build 2143',
  'Shorter hints, fight cues (“It’s jumping!”, “Let go!”, “Ease off!”, “Head shake!”) and messages, same meaning, jokes untouched. Scrap now names the rarity of the Nibbles. The catch card no longer says “dismiss” after an oddity.',
  'Phones: the words that used to be swapped in afterwards (tap, let go) are now written in the game itself; please tell me if any “click” or “Space” shows up anywhere.',
  '## Test build 2035',
  'From your two sweep reports: Market Rush gives its full 30% with the Merchant Path; picking a bait no longer makes the bait buttons jump; tapping a water in Bounties’ sideways row keeps the row where it was (this one is on every build).',
  'iPhone SE size: the top bar no longer cuts “Worms”; when room runs out the chips sit closer together.',
  '## Test build 1943',
  'Menus use much less memory: pictures a page no longer shows are let go at once, and outfit previews share their drawing space. On the iPhone, Run every check ran out of memory during the test suite; it should now finish (the suite itself uses about a quarter of the memory it did, and lets go of each test’s pictures).',
  '## Test build 1832',
  'Tester tools › Run every check: it now runs only this device’s checks (pick iPhone, Android or PC at the top; the game picks for you), carries on if the phone reloads the page partway (before, the run quietly started over and never finished), keeps the screen awake, and Copy report works at any time (it copies what is done so far).',
  '## Test build 1402',
  'Hair: Curly is back to its hand-drawn curls. Under every hat hair now tucks in: nothing bulges out around the brim or pokes up beside the party hat, and big hair sits flat under it. Every style has a light strand texture instead of a flat painted look.',
  'Cherry Blossom Lake, redone: Mount Fuji further away and bigger, with mountains either side; cherry trees with real branches, some weeping; a five-tier pagoda and stone lanterns that glow at night; water lilies; ducks instead of the koi; petals resting and drifting on the water; paper lanterns on the lake at night; now and then a gust carries petals across.',
  'Canadian Rockies, redone: rounded Canadian Shield rocks below the peaks, birches among the pines, a waterfall into a beaver dam and lodge, beavers swimming (one slaps its tail) and gnawing, a moose that stops to drink, Canada geese (and a V flying over), a canoe with a quiet angler, a rebuilt log cabin with the flag, fireweed, clear water showing rocks and weeds, and starry nights with the Milky Way.',
  'Every new water has more life and a moment of its own every half minute or so: dolphins leap at the Florida Keys, a pink river dolphin surfaces in the Amazon, a tractor drives by at Animal Farm, a meatball rolls into the gravy at The Buffet, paper planes and a helicopter at Corporate Pond, a crocodile and a camel caravan on The Nile, drones and glitches at Circuit Lake, Pegasus and an owl on Mount Olympus. Mount Olympus has fuller clouds.',
  'Your home on the new waters: wood choices for the bridge, ledge, stilt deck, hay dock and felucca, and a paint for each home’s best part (Lacquer, Canoe paint, Fence paint, Hull paint, Rim color, Steel finish, Sail color, Neon color, Trim), each named on the page. The Rockies ledge has a new canoe. Until you pick a wood, each home keeps its own natural wood.',
  '## Test build 1042',
  'Menus: picking an option (Wardrobe, pets, Your home, aquarium, Settings) no longer makes the page jump: the option you tapped stays exactly where it was. Trying something on only scrolls to the preview when you can’t already see it.',
  'Fights: a hooked fish turns to swim away when it runs and turns back when it rests.',
  'Jumps: the fish dives first (its shadow sinks, then rushes up) as a warning, Get ready to let go!, then leaps in one arc: nose up out of the water, nose down back in, with a splash both ways.',
  'Swallowed catches: the bigger fish pulls line out steadily for a few seconds instead of all at once. Reeling can’t stop it, only strain the line; rarer fish take more (all of it only for mythics).',
  'Letting go of a running fish drops the tension at once, and only fish over 5 lb take line. Keep reeling instead and it takes no line, but the tension climbs a little faster.',
  'Second wind: a fish with its temper up tires more slowly and may get some strength back (Second wind! shows), a limited number of times by rarity.',
  'Hotspots: the color shows the lowest rarity you’ll catch there (green uncommon, blue rare, purple epic, gold legendary, the rarest); hybrids, shinies and titles come more often in them, and a sparkling hotspot promises a shiny.',
  'Nibbles belong to a rarity now: scrap any common fish to feed any common fish, and so on. Your Nibbles were moved over.',
  'Feeding the aquarium: every fish swims up to the food; each feed may make one fish’s bonuses a little stronger, or now and then give it more income and another bonus.',
  'Prestige: Boardwalk winnings count in full toward Wisdom Pearls. Deep Cooler adds its space again every time your cooler grows. New boon: Strong Arms (Angler strength).',
  'Angler strength: Line upgrades are a little weaker and cost more, and the best Line just matches the strongest fish in the game. New waters cost a little more, and more after each voyage.',
  'Tall sea creatures show whole in the Cooler and other fish pictures (they were cut down to a strip). A gift pet’s belly-rub pose looks more natural.',
  'Every number in the fight and economy changes is a first version: tell me how it feels.',
  'Aquarium › Decorate: the Decorate heading no longer flashes up under the Decorate tab.',
  '## Test build 0912',
  'Stats › Tester tools › Run every check: opens a page that runs every automatic check on this device (about 8 minutes) and puts your test save back. When it finishes, tap Copy report and send it to me.',
  'Split-screen windows: during a live event, the Live button no longer sits under the search button (it steps aside, Events stays in the menu). Also going to the live game with the Tide Pass hotfix.',
  '## Test build 0424',
  'New-water fish: every decoration follows the fish’s real shape: circuit traces differ per fish (no more four dots in a column), ties start at the throat, beaks sit on the nose, horns and ears sit on the head, and nothing covers an eye.',
  'The Cooler / Aquarium button no longer stays on the Fish Log.',
  '## Test build 0403',
  'Nile fish: the striped headdress sits on each fish’s head (no loose piece) and the eye markings never cover the eye.',
  'Tide Pass: the Claim button is back on phones (it was missing, so rewards could not be collected; also going to the live game as a hotfix).',
  'The Cooler / Aquarium button no longer shows as an empty shape on other pages.',
  '## Test build 0342',
  'Cooler: fish a predator swallowed always go into your cooler, even past its limit (they used to be sold).',
  'Wardrobe and pet colors: the color you chose keeps its color and gets a gold box around it (it used to turn solid gold).',
  '## Test build 0330 (your list, part 1)',
  'Fight messages are short now: It’s running!, Careful!, Snagged!, Dead Weight; strong fish say Prepare for a fight, this fish is strong! (or Good luck, this fish is out of your league! when it is 10+ stronger than you).',
  'A missed bite keeps your line out; the 5th miss in a row reels in. Reeled in early and Missed a bite say just that. Cast power keeps its words over a hotspot, only its color changes.',
  'Bait: three groups (Everyday bait, Water baits, Favourite foods), each sorted by price; they open folded, tap a group to open it. Cooler: Sort (Newest, Oldest, Sell value, Aquarium bonus, Species) and Scrap all (same filters as Sell all).',
  'Also: shorter Heavy fog text and a Weather pop-ups switch in Settings, Stickleback has a new line, only cats purr, oddities and other non-fish say dismiss instead of the cooler line, the three treasure chests sit inside their pop-up.',
  'Phones: a Cooler / Aquarium button beside Settings switches between the two; the aquarium button now reads Expand Tank with the next size under it.',
  '## Fixes earlier in 0.4.9',
  'Deep QC round: 30 fish renamed so no two share a name; attachment stats no longer read “undefined”; oddity names wrap on small PC windows.',
  'Second QC round (looks): the Tide Pass page shows this chapter’s exclusives as pictures plus progress for every chapter; a new Wardrobe tab to wear auras, bobbers and lines; Paths is shorter and uses two columns on wide screens; path fees are round numbers; Boons fill the whole width; end-game waters get their own heading.',
  'Top bar Bait chip, fixed properly this time (the first fix did not work): with a live event on, Tasks and then the event chip make room before Bait ever shortens.',
  'Code cleanup: about 260 lines of old code that could never run are gone (each build is about 40 KB smaller), the aquarium no longer re-sorts its fish every frame, and a reeling safety check was added. Nothing should look or play differently.',
  'Fixed: a game with a Path chosen could freeze while starting (black water, nothing reacts to taps).',
  'Behind the scenes: Android and iPhone now share one set of patch notes. Nothing should look or play differently.',
  '## What the 0.4.9 big patch adds',
  'Paths (15, ranks I–V, Remove + fee on each fork), Prestige: Pearl shop, Boons, 32 milestones, 21 relics.',
  'Boardwalk: Fishmonger’s Gamble and Treasure chests. Tide Pass: 100 levels, chapters, exclusives (Wardrobe › Tide Pass exclusives).',
  'New waters: Cherry Blossom (after Stonebrook), Rockies (after Frostbite), Keys (after Coral), Amazon (after Brine Shelf). End-game waters open by voyage (Stats › tester tools can add voyages).',
  '300 oddities: rarity and odds show only once found (tap a found one).',
  'Looks: reel hand + left-handed (Settings › Display), Natural face + new hair/noses/mouths/eye shapes (Wardrobe), new fish eyes, wizard hat, pet colors.',
  'Fight rework: fish must be tired out; holding through rare runs snaps the line. Times with maxed gear: ~2.5 s common to ~36 s mythic.',
  'Fishing: try holding reel through a rare fish’s runs (it should snap), then let go when it runs (it should land).',
  'Aquarium fish show real sizes and depth; hair rebuilt with volume (all 20 styles); body builds have distinct silhouettes; smaller noses on the Natural face.',
  'Please test on every platform and send me anything that feels off.']};
addTestNotes(TEST_NOTES);
